<title>AUSTRIA: BIATHLON-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BIATHLON-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROSENAU-WINDISCHGARSTEN, Austria 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results</p>
<p>in the European Biathlon championships on Sunday:</p>
<p>Men's 4x7.5 km relay</p>
<p>1. Germany (Ulf Karkoschka/Holger Schoenthier/Lars</p>
<p>Kreuzer/Marco Morgenstern) 1 hour 21 minutes 31.7 seconds (no</p>
<p>penalty laps)</p>
<p>2. Russia (Vladimir Bekhterev/Andrei Padine/Alexei Sidorov/</p>
<p>Eduard Riabov) 1:22:10.2 (one lap)</p>
<p>3. Norway (Stig-Are Eriksen/Kjetil Saeter/Lars Sigve Oftedal/</p>
<p>Kjell Ove Oftedal) 1:23:12.9 (no laps)</p>
<p>4. Italy 1:23:13.0 (no laps)</p>
<p>5. Belarus 1:23:34.6 (no laps)</p>
<p>6. France 1:23:43.5 (two laps)</p>
<p>Women's 3x7.5 km relay</p>
<p>1. Russia (Irina Mileschina/Tatiana Martynova/Albina Achatova)</p>
<p>1:28:34.2 (two laps)</p>
<p>2. Germany (Katja Beer/Janet Klein/Steffi Kindt) 1:29:35.5 (two</p>
<p>laps)</p>
<p>3. Czech Republic (Irena Madlova/Jitka Simunkova/Irena Tomsova)</p>
<p>1:30:01.3 (no laps)</p>
<p>4. Norway 1:32:48.4 (three laps)</p>
<p>5. Ukraine 1:32:49.6 (one lap)</p>
<p>6. Bulgaria 1:33:22.8 (four laps)</p>
</text>
